  "attempt": "For an accelerated Collatz valuation word a_1,...,a_m, write T^m(n)=(3^m n+C_a)/2^S. If every reverse suffix of length k has valuation sum at least qk for an integer q>=2, then C_a/(2^S-3^m)<=1/(2^q-3). In particular q=2 forces T^m(n)<n for every odd n>1 realizing the word. Under the exact geometric cylinder law, the mass of q=2 certificate words of length m is binom(2m,m)/4^m, which tends to zero. Moreover, for a fixed valuation multiset, ascending order minimizes C_a and descending order maximizes it. Thus final surplus S-m log_2 3 alone cannot control the affine threshold.",
