    "declared_proposition": "For an accelerated Collatz valuation word a_1,...,a_m, write T^m(n)=(3^m n+C_a)/2^S. If every reverse suffix of length k has valuation sum at least qk for an integer q>=2, then C_a/(2^S-3^m)<=1/(2^q-3). In particular q=2 forces T^m(n)<n for every odd n>1 realizing the word. Under the exact geometric cylinder law, the mass of q=2 certificate words of length m is binom(2m,m)/4^m, which tends to zero. Moreover, for a fixed valuation multiset, ascending order minimizes C_a and descending order maximizes it. Thus final surplus S-m log_2 3 alone cannot control the affine threshold.",
    "mathematical_argument": "The affine constant is C_a=sum_{j=0}^{m-1}3^(m-1-j)2^S_j. Divide by 2^S and index by reverse suffix length k. The suffix hypothesis bounds the k-th term by 3^(k-1)/2^(qk); summing the geometric series and comparing with 1-3^m/2^S gives the threshold bound. For the mass formula, reverse the i.i.d. geometric valuations and apply the skip-free ballot identity to increments a_i-2. For ordering, an adjacent swap changes only one prefix term; putting the larger valuation first increases that term.",
